// Title: Potential Linux Amazon SSM Agent Hijacking
// Sigma ID: f9b3edc5-3322-4fc7-8aa3-245d646cc4b7
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Muhammad Faisal
// Date: 2023-08-03 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, persistence, T1219.002
// Description: Detects potential Amazon SSM agent hijack attempts as outlined in the Mitiga research report.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate activity of system administrators
// References:
//   - https://www.mitiga.io/blog/mitiga-security-advisory-abusing-the-ssm-agent-as-a-remote-access-trojan
//   - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/amazons-aws-ssm-agent-can-be-used-as-post-exploitation-rat-malware/
//   - https://www.helpnetsecurity.com/2023/08/02/aws-instances-attackers-access/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_ssm_agent_abuse.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/amazon-ssm-agent" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "-register " and ProcessCommandLine contains "-code " and ProcessCommandLine contains "-id " and ProcessCommandLine contains "-region ")
